[{"id":79944,"sender_id":781,"sender_full_name":"chase cain","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ff453977d5894ba2970960bac77ebc81?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/universal.20Cat-bundles/near/79944\">#1</a> I’m currently wrestling with the ideas in the following two pages:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Grothendieck%2Bconstruction\">Grothendieck+construction</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/generalized%2Buniversal%2Bbundles\">generalized+universal+bundles</a></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Here are the specifics: In [1] the Grothendieck construction is described as the (strict) pullback of the universal Cat-bundle <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Cat}_{\\ast,\\ell}\\to\\operatorname{Cat}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∗</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span></span></span>. In [2], under the section “<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>-subobject classifiers” is the statement:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\mathrm{pt}}\\operatorname{Cat}\\to\\operatorname{Cat}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">pt</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span></span></span> is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Cat}_*\\to\\operatorname{Cat}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1757em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span></span></span>. Pullback of this gives the Grothendieck construction.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Of course, the categories <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Cat}_*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1757em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Cat}_{\\ast,\\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∗</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> are slightly different, only in the morphisms. My question is: can the category <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Cat}_{\\ast,\\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∗</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> be described as some variation of the pullback:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>I</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>←</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">?</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\mathrm{pt}}\\operatorname{Cat} = \\lim([I,\\operatorname{Cat}]\\to\\operatorname{Cat}\\leftarrow {\\mathrm{pt}}) = \\operatorname{Cat}_*?</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">pt</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lim</span><span class=\"mopen\">([</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">←</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">pt</span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1757em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">?</span></span></span></span></span></p>","timestamp":1574357448,"subject":"universal Cat-bundles","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]